All regular board meetings should follow an established order of business. The order is as follows:
(1) Call to order;
(2) Invocation and pledge of allegiance;
(3) Approval of minutes;
(4) Citizens having business with the county;
(5) List of unpaid invoices;
(6) Tax reliefs;
(7) Commission business;
(8) County administrator;
(9) County attorney;
(10) Public comments; and
(11) Adjournment.
